    # --- CAND-034 -------------------------------------------------------------
    # The 136 codes that reached the operator as "Research command failed." while
    # the reason was known, static, and safe to show.
    #
    # The wording is not invented here. `preflight_freeze`, `opt_in_policy` and
    # `call_plan` were mapped independently and converged on the same five slots:
    # four shared messages -- identifier, malformed, unsupported schema, not
    # found -- plus one sentence naming the artifact, which carries most of a
    # family's codes. These entries follow that, so 136 codes needed 13 new
    # sentences rather than 136.
    #
    # The status stays per-code where the message is shared across a family: the
    # status is the machine-readable detail a client switches on, the message is
    # what a human reads, and the two are deliberately not the same granularity.
    #
    # These are literals, matched exactly. Nothing is derived from the code at
    # runtime -- 33 raise sites build their code with an f-string, and a pattern
    # rule would echo whatever string arrived. Those still land on the generic
    # fallback, which is the fail-safe half of this design and stays.
